  "description": "Dear Team,\n\nPlease find below the current overview of our OpenStack\u2011related personnel, releases, companies, repositories and project classifications. Alice Smith (launchpad ID **alice.smith**, Gerrit ID **aliceg**) can be reached at **alice.smith@example.com** and is presently affiliated with **Acme Corp**, which she will leave on **2024-Dec-31**. Bob Jones (launchpad ID **bob-jones**) uses the email addresses **bob_jones@openstack.org** and **bob.jones@acme.com** and is currently employed by the **OpenStack Foundation** with no end date specified.\n\nOur roadmap includes two major releases: **v1.0**, scheduled to conclude on **2025-Mar-15**, and **v2.0**, slated for **2026-Jun-30**. The partner companies involved are **Acme Corp** (domains: **acme.com**, **acme.org**) and the **OpenStack Foundation** (domains: **openstack.org**, **openstack.com**).\n\nThe Nova source code resides at **https://github.com/openstack/nova.git**, under the **openstack** organization and the **nova** module. For release **v1.0** it tracks branch **stable/2024.1**, moving from tag **17.0.0** to **18.0.0**; for release **v2.0** it progresses from tag **18.0.0** to **19.0.0** (no branch recorded). Project types are categorized as follows: the **service** type (ID **service**, not a child, titled **Service Projects**) includes the modules **nova**, **cinder**, and **neutron**; the **library** type (ID **library**, marked as a child, titled **Library Projects**) comprises **python-openstackclient** and **python-novaclient**."
